A||N||4||bHooper||VIR, Motorola Cup and a Fiero||||10||
Z||000000||bHooper||09-18-2000||09:48 AM||||Yesterday, my girlfriend and I drove up to Virginia International Raceway to watch the Mororola Cup race.  It was a beautiful fall day, so we decided to take the Fiero (this would be it's first long trip since putting her back together in May).<P>For those of you not familiar with VIR, it was built in the 50's, and used to host a lot of races.  Closed in the 70's, a company bought it, several years ago, rebuilt the track and turned it into a "country club" for racers! <A HREF="http://www.virclub.com/files/indexnow.cfm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.virclub.com/files/indexnow.cfm</A> <P>After the race was over, they let us take "touring laps" of the track... <B>WOW!!!!</B> that was fun!  Didn't get to go as fast as I woulda liked, they had a pace car in front (which made my girlfriend very happy), but we were able to ride the line at about 50 mph... and get the feel of the track!<P>It definatly makes you feel good, driving around a track like that!<P>Oh yea, it was also very surprising, the number of people that would look at my Fiero (even though it aint pretty, right now) with a curious look on their face  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I had fun!<BR>(sorry for the length of the post, but i had to share my day with everyone)<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||10
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-18-2000||10:22 AM||||Cool, hoop!  I checked the VIR site and looked thru the pictures of the track.  That had to have been a riot even at 50mph!<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">       <BR>       <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||bHooper||09-18-2000||10:41 AM||||It was!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>We drove the north course.  Unfortunately, the car in front of me was a Olds Intrigue, drivin by a young girl (early 20's) with her grandparents in the back seat!  She drove terrible slow, and always off line (like she was on the street).<P>In front of her, was a Cobra... but he tried to show off on the front strait and broke something <B>KLANK!</B><P>My buddy in his tricked out Mercedes 190 2.4l 16v (near race car), with 15" front brakes, caused a guy to spin his 3000GT off into the dirt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">.<P>That was so fun!... I can't wait to get my suspension fixed and start taking some lessons!<P>The best thing, is in the heart of NASTYCAR country... we now have one of the nicest road tracks in america, just 45 min from my home!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||09-18-2000||11:45 AM||||I'm jealous, bHooper.  Fiero + road course = lots and lots of fun.<P>Hey, FOCOA's national meet is going to be in Williamsburg, VA next year.  Sure would be cool if we could work out some kind of on-track event at VIR...||||reg||3
Z||000004||bHooper||09-18-2000||01:01 PM||||Really?!... the main FOCOA event for 2001 is on the east coast?  I have to get busy!  The GT needs paint, suspension, brakes, exhaust, and tires.<P>Yes, VIR would be a perfect place to run, although I dont know how far it is from wiliamsburgh.<P>Someone told me, that the track might even be in the running for a future CART race!  But it needs to widen the track and build grandstands (it doesnt provide any seating at the moment).<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
